#HELPS

0 FANGS CLAWS NATURALWEAPONS~
Syntax: fangs
        claws
Toggles the eligible character's native natural-weapon flags.
Vampire claws require Protean 2; Werewolf claws follow native form
and gift rules. These are not free permanent weapon-skill increases.
Use UPKEEP to inspect the resulting state and your class help for
special claw passives or attacks.
~

0 NIGHTSIGHT DARKVISION HEIGHTEN UMBRALVISION SHAREDSIGHT~
Shared sight commands keep their class-specific prerequisites:
  NIGHTSIGHT or DARKVISION: toggles native darkvision.
  HEIGHTEN: toggles enhanced sight/detection.
  UMBRALVISION: toggles shadow sight; it does not move you into Umbra.
Vampire examples are Protean 1 for Nightsight and Auspex 1 for Heighten.
Werewolf examples are Metis 3 for Nightsight and Lupus 1 for Heighten.
Drow and other supported classes retain their own learned-power gates.
Sight powers are not staff HOLYLIGHT permissions or class conversion.
~

0 SCRY READAURA LIFESCAN REMOTEKNOWLEDGE~
Syntax: scry <target>
        readaura <target>
LIFESCAN is an alias for READAURA, not a separate alignment spell.
SCRY examines an eligible distant location; READAURA examines a
creature's native aura/stat information, subject to wards and concealment.
Vampires need Auspex 3 for Scry and 2 for Read Aura. Werewolves use
Lupus 2 for Scry or Glass Walkers 2 for Read Aura; Monks use Mantra 2.
Drow and other supported classes retain their own learned-power gates.
Soul Mask can falsify aura presentation; this does not alter real stats.
~

0 AWE MAJESTY VAMPIREPRESENCE~
Vampire Presence toggles:
  1 AWE: native awe/charisma state.
  5 MAJESTY: native peace/majesty state with its normal combat checks.
Werewolf Homid persuasion uses PERSUASION, not a free Presence grant.
These powers do not train Presence or permanently modify base stats.
Related: DREADGAZE, ENTRANCEMENT, SUMMONING, ENRAGE, UPKEEP.
~

0 DREADGAZE ENTRANCEMENT SUMMONING PRESENCEACTIONS~
Vampire Presence actions:
  2 DREADGAZE <target>: attempts the native fear/disruption effect.
  3 ENTRANCEMENT <target>: attempts native fascination/charm.
  4 SUMMONING <target>: calls an eligible creature to the caster.
These retain their distinct target, consent, resistance and protection
checks. SUMMONING moves the target; it is not the caster's own travel.
Other parents' similarly named powers retain their own class interfaces.
~

0 MASK TRUEDISGUISE VAMPIREDISGUISES~
Syntax: mask <target>
        truedisguise <target>
Vampire MASK requires Obfuscate 2; TRUEDISGUISE requires Chimerstry 6.
They use the native disguise/form mechanisms and their own eligible
targets. Reusing an active disguise follows the native removal path.
Disguises do not rename your account or grant the target's staff role.
Do not confuse them with cloning objects or enrolling in another class.
~

0 CHANGE SERPENT VAMPIRESHAPES~
Syntax: change <bat|wolf|mist|human>
        serpent
CHANGE requires Vampire Protean 4; SERPENT requires Serpentis 4.
These use the native polymorph system. Mist requires its additional
native Protean gate and uses the ethereal/mist state; HUMAN removes
the CHANGE forms through their native cleanup.
SERPENT toggles its own form. Conflicting forms retain their checks.
These shapes do not grant another standalone parent's complete kit.
~

0 SOULMASK FALSEAURA~
Syntax: soulmask
        soulmask <on|off>
        soulmask <skill|stance|hit|dam|ac|hp|max_hp> <value>
Requires Vampire Obfuscate 5. With no argument, displays the current
mask values and configurable fields.
The mask changes the native aura/stat presentation seen by others.
It does not change real maximum health, armor, damage or learned ranks.
Values must satisfy the native field validation.
~

0 VANISH OBFUSCATECONCEALMENT~
Syntax: vanish
        vanish all
Requires Vampire Obfuscate 1 for the caster's concealment.
The ALL variant requires Obfuscate 3 and uses native group concealment.
This applies the native obfuscation flag, not staff invisibility.
Combat/detection rules can expose you; it is not invulnerability.
~

0 EARTHMELD VAMPIREMELD~
Syntax: earthmeld
Requires Vampire Protean 3. Toggles the native earthmeld state,
including its normal environmental/form restrictions.
Protean 6 EARTHSHIFT requires this state before underground travel.
Earthmelding is not automatic permission to bypass protected rooms.
~

0 UMBRA SHADOWPLANE~
Syntax: umbra
Attempts the character's native shadow-plane transition, subject to
its existing entry restrictions.
This changes plane state, unlike UMBRALVISION which changes sight only.
Mage STEP SIDEWAYS and BREAK DREAMSHELL are separate sphere abilities.
Related: UMBRALVISION, GRASP, REACH, STEP SIDEWAYS.
~

0 DEFENCES DEFENSECONSENT~
Syntax: defences
Toggles the native raised/lowered-defences consent state.
Lowering defences permits certain feeding, teaching, embrace or clan
interactions when their other requirements are met.
This flag is not an armor trainer, an invulnerability toggle or a
permanent increase to combat stats. Raise it again when finished.
~

0 REGENERATE FEED VAMPIRERECOVERY~
Syntax: regenerate
        feed <target>
REGENERATE invokes the native recovery/regrowth routine with its
existing injury and resource checks.
The legacy Vampire FEED action draws blood from an eligible target.
Player targets retain native consent/defence requirements.
Neither command creates a new permanent parent class or automatically
maximizes your stats. Other parents' recovery powers use their own menus.
~

0 FLEX ESCAPEBONDS~
Syntax: flex
Attempts to break native physical bindings, webs or shadow tendrils
when their individual checks permit it, and applies an action delay.
It is not a universal dispel of every magical root or scripted prison.
Travel still checks any restraints or effects that remain afterward.
~

0 RAGE CALM WOLFRAGE~
Syntax: rage
        calm
Werewolf RAGE increases current rage and can trigger the native wolf
transformation; it does not train permanent Rage.
Werewolf CALM requires Children of Gaia 1 and reduces native rage.
Ninja CALM ends active Michi through its own native path.
Other classes do not gain those states merely by knowing the command.
~

0 UPKEEP POWERS~
Syntax: upkeep
        powers
UPKEEP displays the native active powers and resource/upkeep state.
POWERS displays unlocked command powers for its supported class route;
it is not a trainer or an automatic grant of every ability.
Werewolves use WWPOWERS/WWUPKEEP, Drow use DROWPOWERS/DROWUPKEEP,
and Monks use MONKLEARN. New parents also supply their own class menus.
Related: DISCIPLINE, ELEMSKILL, PRINCIPLE, MONKLEARN.
~

0 DISCIPLINE TEACHDISC VAMPIRETRAINING~
Syntax: discipline
        discipline <discipline name>
        teachdisc <person> <discipline name>
DISCIPLINE displays or trains the Vampire's learned discipline tracks.
The native clan/non-clan caps, knowledge requirements and primal costs
still apply. Knowing a command name does not train its discipline.
TEACHDISC attempts to teach an eligible recipient using the existing
teacher, recipient, consent and learning-cost checks.
It is not a hybrid selector or a way to bypass staff permissions.
~

0 PIGEON BECKONING ANIMALCOMMANDS~
Syntax: pigeon <player> <message>
        beckoning <animal>
Vampire PIGEON requires Animalism 1 and uses the native messenger.
BECKONING requires Vampire Animalism 2 or Werewolf Lupus 4.
Native choices include horse/stallion/mount, frog, raven, dog, cat,
molerat and yak. Summoned creatures use native follower ownership.
This is not unrestricted mobile creation or a player teleport command.
~

0 BEASTWITHIN SERENITY SONGSERENITY ANIMALINFLUENCE~
Syntax: beastwithin <target>
        serenity <target>
SONGSERENITY is an alias for SERENITY.
Vampire BEASTWITHIN requires Animalism 4 and attempts to provoke the
target's native beast/rage response.
Vampire SERENITY requires Animalism 3; Werewolf Children of Gaia 4
also has its native Serenity route.
These retain target eligibility, resistance and protective checks.
~

0 UNVEIL EMBRACE POSSESSION VAMPIREINTERACTIONS~
Syntax: unveil <target>
        embrace <target>
        possession <target>
Vampire UNVEIL requires Auspex 4 and attempts the native revealing
interaction. EMBRACE uses native grapple/embrace conditions, including
the applicable class, generation, defence and blood restrictions.
POSSESSION uses Dominate and its own target/level/connection gates.
These are distinct interactions, not permission to select any class
or act as an administrator. Use RETURN after a successful body switch.
~

0 MIRRORIMAGE FORMILLUSION ILLUSIONARYFORM CLONEOBJECT ILLUSIONCREATION~
Vampire Chimerstry commands:
  1 MIRRORIMAGE: creates the native mirror-image illusion.
  2 FORMILLUSION <target>: creates the native creature-form illusion.
  3 CLONEOBJECT <object>: creates the native temporary object clone.
ILLUSIONARYFORM is an alias for FORMILLUSION.
Werewolf Fianna uses 3 for Form Illusion and 4 for Clone Object.
Illusory objects use native vanishing/timer rules; they are not
permanent duplicates of another player's artifact collection.
~

0 FALSEAPPEARANCE CONTROLILLUSION ILLUSIONEDITING~
Syntax: falseappearance <object> rename <short description>
        falseappearance <object> keyword <extra keywords>
        controlillusion <illusion> <command>
Vampire FALSEAPPEARANCE requires Chimerstry 4 and edits an eligible
object's native presentation, not its underlying account permissions.
CONTROLILLUSION requires Chimerstry 5 and directs an eligible illusion
through its existing ownership and command checks.
These do not enroll a new character or create arbitrary staff actors.
~

0 OMNIPOTENCE REMOTEEYE~
Syntax: omnipotence <target>
        omnipotence
The legacy Vampire route requires Auspex 6 and uses the native remote
eye/projection system. Other supported routes keep their own gates.
This is a perception/control ability, not administrator access or
unrestricted invulnerability. With an active eye, the no-argument
variant dismisses it. Associated familiar commands retain
their ownership and occupied-body checks.
~

0 THINBLOOD QUIETUSDEBUFF~
Syntax: thinblood <target>
Requires Vampire Quietus 6 and an eligible nearby target.
Applies the native thin-blood debuff with its resource, resistance
and duplicate checks. It does not permanently change account class.
Related: LEECH, DISCIPLINE, UPKEEP.
~

0 OUTCAST FAVOUR CLANMEMBERSHIP~
Syntax: outcast <target>
        favour <target> <elder|induct|outcast>
OUTCAST routes Ninja clan outcasting through its existing rank rules.
Vampires and Werewolves use the appropriate FAVOUR membership route
and its legacy class/clan/generation checks instead.
These are not the future universal ClassLeader or hybrid permissions.
Monks use DECIDE/EXPEL for their own legacy clan operations.
~

0 CLANNAME STAFFCLANNAME~
Syntax: clanname <player> [new clan name]
Staff-only clan-name editor, registered at LEV_IMM.
Changes the selected player's clan string to at most 25 characters.
Leaving the new name blank clears it. This is not a player clan
creation command and does not grant class or staff permissions.
~

0 FAMILIAR STAFFFAMILIARBINDING~
Syntax: familiar <creature>
        familiar clear
Staff-only helper, registered at LEV_IMP and checked again by the handler.
Binds only the caller's own charmed, unclaimed NPC follower here.
Players and occupied/switched NPC bodies cannot be bound.
CLEAR releases the familiar link, not the underlying follower itself.
This does not spawn an NPC or add a new power to ordinary player kits.
~

0 [ FAMILIARCONTROL~
Syntax: [ <command>
Directs the character's associated, owned, unoccupied NPC familiar.
The native forbidden-action and silence checks remain in force.
An NPC currently occupied/switched by a live connection cannot be
commanded through this interface. It does not borrow that user's trust.
Normal NPC command permissions apply; this is not staff FORCE.
~

0 AUTOCLASS CLASSENROLLMENT~
Syntax: autoclass
        autoclass <class> [clan/tradition/color]
Displays choices or enrolls a qualified unclassed character through
the native class-selection rules. Vampire clan, Mage tradition and
Dragon color have their existing additional selection rules.
The legacy Elemental selector is named ELEMENTALIST.
SORCERER CHAOS, CHAOSMAGE and CHAOSBOOKMAGE select the Chaos book variant.
New parents use their own documented names. This command is not
remort/respec, hybrid activation or pure-class ascension.
Related: CLASS, BOOKMAGIC, HYBRIDROSTER.
~

0 $~
